  "proven": [
    "Actual Console production assets enter through the Workspace publishing link; BFF resolves the session, validates CSRF and exact authorization, and forwards the returned authorization context plus stable idempotency identity.",
    "Real HTTP BFF, Capability signed multipart and restricted owner databases execute Package upload and Build admission; browser-body actor injection, missing session, wrong CSRF, cross-origin writes and cross-tenant reads are rejected.",
    "Browser-driven real BuildKit/Registry output reaches a ready CapabilityVersion with matching immutable artifact digest, and reload reads the same result. Desktop/mobile screenshots were inspected.",
    "Ledger records package.uploaded, build.artifact_confirmed/build.failed and capability.version_registered through authenticated typed events in the existing receipt store. Real PostgreSQL tests prove replay after lost acknowledgements, producer binding and rejection of changed bytes for the same event identity.",
    "An actually admitted worker runs in a separate OS process. A test-only docker wrapper lets the real exporter commit to Registry but withholds its exit acknowledgement; SIGKILL terminates the worker. A fresh worker/database connection, configured with an unusable builder, recovers the original digest to one artifact/event/version without rerunning export."
  ],
  "notProven": [
